+++ turret_host/config.py
@@ -864,6 +864,75 @@
 # 30 fps this is ~4 frames, enough to ride out a dropped frame without letting a
 # tracker coast the beam across a room on a stale measurement.
 DRONE_BOX_MAX_AGE_S = 0.150
+
+#: How long the tracker keeps offering the last ASSOCIATED detection to the
+#: interlock after a frame that failed to associate. 0.0 restores the old
+#: behaviour (the box is dropped on the first miss).
+#:
+#: WHY IT EXISTS. 32 of the 62 raw firing bursts in run_2026-09-20_145109 ended
+#: on `drone_lock` alone -- one detector miss, beam off, beam on again a frame
+#: later. The detection was good, the drone had not moved, and nothing about
+#: the permission had actually changed; only the detector blinked.
+#:
+#: WHY IT IS SAFE. The held box carries its ORIGINAL box_t, so
+#: DRONE_BOX_MAX_AGE_S still rejects it by age and the containment test still
+#: runs against the CURRENT aim point every frame. A drone that moves away from
+#: the beam loses containment on the next frame exactly as before. This extends
+#: how long a measurement stays usable; it does not make a stale measurement
+#: count as a fresh one.
+#:
+#: 0.100 is three frames at 30 fps, and is bounded by DRONE_BOX_MAX_AGE_S
+#: (0.150) regardless.
+#:
+#: MEASURED, AND IT IS A REGRESSION ON ITS OWN. Replay of 145109 (see
+#: tools/replay_gates.py): raw bursts 62 -> 40, which is the fragmentation this
+#: is meant to fix -- but FIRING rows 638 -> 567 and beam time 21.0 -> 18.7 s,
+#: because the longer continuous bursts reach LASER_MAX_ON_MS (2000) sooner and
+#: each cap costs a LASER_COOLDOWN_S rest. Duty trips go 1 -> 3 and rows lost to
+#: cool-down 52 -> 159. With the duty cap relaxed to 5000/500 ms the same hold
+#: gives 729 rows and 24.0 s. SO: DO NOT SHIP THIS WITHOUT THE DUTY CHANGE.
+FIRE_BOX_HOLD_S = 0.100
+
+# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
+#   ASSOCIATION-TIME SHAPE AND LONE-DETECTION RULES  (item 4)
+# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
+#: Reject a detection as a MEASUREMENT when it is this much wider than tall.
+#:
+#: THE HAND SIGNATURE IS SPECIFICALLY WIDE, AND ONLY WIDE. On
+#: run_2026-09-20_145109 the turret converged on hand-shaped boxes for 1.07 s
+#: (f006805-f006835, 17 associated boxes, aspect 1.67-2.22) before firing on
+#: the carrier's knuckles. Blocking those at the INTERLOCK stops the beam;
+#: blocking them HERE stops the aim point being dragged onto the hand in the
+#: first place, which is the thing that made a coincidence of gates dangerous.
+#:
+#: DELIBERATELY ASYMMETRIC, AND THIS IS THE WHOLE POINT. There is no low bound.
+#: The drone held edge-on or folded produces a TALL NARROW box -- measured at
+#: aspect 0.39-0.48 on 17 frames across both runs, and the frames show the real
+#: airframe every time (145109 f004546, f004638, f005092; 144709 f002569,
+#: f003527). Applying FIRE_BOX_ASPECT_MIN (0.45) here would throw those away
+#: and lose the track, which is exactly the failure item 4 exists to reduce.
+#: The firing gate may be symmetric because refusing to fire is free; refusing
+#: to ASSOCIATE is not.
+#:
+#: Cost, measured across both runs: of the 55 accepted boxes outside the firing
+#: window, this rule rejects the 27 wide ones (25 of them the hand cluster) and
+#: keeps all 28 narrow ones.
+ASSOC_BOX_ASPECT_MAX = 1.6
+
+#: A lone confident detection this far from the prediction is accepted even
+#: though the covariance gate refused it.
+#:
+#: In run_2026-09-20_144709, 21 of 26 TRACK losses were the real drone --
+#: conf 0.54-0.81, median 241 px from the prediction -- discarded because the
+#: carrier moved faster than the filter expected. With one detection in frame
+#: and nothing else to confuse it with, "far from where I predicted" is
+#: evidence the PREDICTION is wrong, not that the detection is.
+#:
+#: Guarded three ways: only when it is the ONLY detection in the frame, only
+#: above ASSOC_LONE_CONF, and only when the box is drone-shaped by the rule
+#: above. GATE_MAX_PX (300) still caps everything.
+ASSOC_LONE_PX = 250.0
+ASSOC_LONE_CONF = 0.5
 # Shrink the box per side before testing containment, as a fraction of its own
 # width/height so it scales with range. The 283 mm airframe is ~132 px at 3 m,
 # so 0.15 leaves ~92 px of permitted region there -- the body, not the rim,
